    <h3 id="upload-api-ticket-title">Implement a new internal upload API</h3>
  </header>
  <div class="tracking-ticket-body">
    <section>
      <h4>Required behavior</h4>
      <p>Allow internal clients to upload PDF files up to 15 MB. Reject unsupported files and uploads above the size limit.</p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h4>Constraints</h4>
      <p>Reuse the existing authentication middleware. Use the legacy transport layer by default, with transport selection behind a feature toggle so we can enable the new transport when it is ready.</p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h4>Operating expectations</h4>
      <p>Include the endpoint in the existing internal SLO. Expect an average of 3,000 requests per minute and a peak of 300 concurrent requests.</p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h4>Out of scope</h4>
      <p>Implementing the new transport layer is a separate ticket. This change prepares its rollout through the feature toggle.</p>
      <p>Do not refactor the existing API. We’ll deprecate it in a separate PR once the new API is fully rolled out.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
  <footer class="tracking-ticket-footer">
    <svg class="tracking-ticket-rule" viewBox="0 0 508 6" preserveAspectRatio="none" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M2 3Q126 1 254 3T506 2" vector-effect="non-scaling-stroke"/></svg>
